Drop jsp-likely-xss: it declares `mode: join`, which the OpenGrep engine this
product ships does not support, so `opengrep validate` rejects the catalog.

The rule is not rewritten here. Join mode correlates a metavariable across two
independent sub-rules anywhere in a file; a single-pattern approximation is a
different rule, and shipping one under upstream's id and message would report
findings that upstream's rule did not make. The narrower check lives in
rules/lycaon/jsp/security.yaml under a first-party id instead.

diff --git a/rules/generic/jsp-likely-xss.yaml b/rules/generic/jsp-likely-xss.yaml
deleted file mode 100644
